#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:9
msgid ""
"This is a large database of mime types and information about them. It "
"consists of a single, public JSON file and does not include any logic, "
"allowing it to remain as un-opinionated as possible with an API. It "
"aggregates data from the following sources:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:14
msgid "http://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/media-types.xhtml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:15
msgid "http://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/httpd/httpd/trunk/docs/conf/mime.types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:16
msgid "http://hg.nginx.org/nginx/raw-file/default/conf/mime.types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:18
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:24
msgid "Database Download"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:26
msgid ""
"If you're crazy enough to use this in the browser, you can just grab the "
"JSON file using [jsDelivr](https://www.jsdelivr.com/). It is recommended "
"to replace `master` with [a release tag](https://github.com/jshttp/mime-"
"db/tags) as the JSON format may change in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:35
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:44
msgid "Data Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:46
msgid ""
"The JSON file is a map lookup for lowercased mime types. Each mime type "
"has the following properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:49
msgid ""
"`.source` - where the mime type is defined.   If not set, it's probably a"
" custom media type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:51
msgid ""
"`apache` - [Apache common media "
"types](http://svn.apache.org/repos/asf/httpd/httpd/trunk/docs/conf/mime.types)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:52
msgid ""
"`iana` - [IANA-defined media types](http://www.iana.org/assignments"
"/media-types/media-types.xhtml)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:53
msgid ""
"`nginx` - [nginx media types](http://hg.nginx.org/nginx/raw-"
"file/default/conf/mime.types)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:54
msgid "`.extensions[]` - known extensions associated with this mime type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:55
msgid "`.compressible` - whether a file of this type can be gzipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:56
msgid "`.charset` - the default charset associated with this type, if any."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:58
msgid "If unknown, every property could be `undefined`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:60
msgid "Contributing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:62
msgid ""
"To edit the database, only make PRs against `src/custom-types.json` or "
"`src/custom-suffix.json`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:65
msgid ""
"The `src/custom-types.json` file is a JSON object with the MIME type as "
"the keys and the values being an object with the following keys:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:68
msgid ""
"`compressible` - leave out if you don't know, otherwise `true`/`false` to"
" indicate whether the data represented by the type is typically "
"compressible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:70
msgid ""
"`extensions` - include an array of file extensions that are associated "
"with the type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:72
msgid "`notes` - human-readable notes about the type, typically what the type is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:73
msgid ""
"`sources` - include an array of URLs of where the MIME type and the "
"associated extensions are sourced from. This needs to be a [primary "
"source](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primary_source); links to type "
"aggregating sites and Wikipedia are _not acceptable_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:77
msgid "To update the build, run `npm run build`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:79
msgid "Adding Custom Media Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:81
msgid ""
"The best way to get new media types included in this library is to "
"register them with the IANA. The community registration procedure is "
"outlined in [RFC 6838 section "
"5](http://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc6838#section-5). Types registered with "
"the IANA are automatically pulled into this library."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/mime-db_README.md:86
msgid ""
"If that is not possible / feasible, they can be added directly here as a "
"\"custom\" type. To do this, it is required to have a primary source that"
" definitively lists the media type. If an extension is going to be listed"
" as associateed with this media type, the source must definitively link "
"the media type and extension as well."
msgstr ""

